{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgfv6EjJckMgAqJCxdxVW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 1700 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 640 cm⁻¹**\n\n**Assignment.** The ground state is ³T₁g(F). The three spin-allowed bands are:\n- ν₁ = ³T₁g(F) → ³T₂g\n- ν₂ = ³T₁g(F) → ³T₁g(P)\n- ν₃ = ³T₁g(F) → ³A₂g\n\n**Energies, with ³F at zero.**\n- ³T₂g lies at 2Dq.\n- ³A₂g lies at 12Dq.\n- The two ³T₁g states mix through the matrix [[−6Dq, 4Dq], [4Dq, 15B]]. Its eigenvalues are E₋ (the ground state) and E₊ (³T₁g(P)).\n\nThis matrix gives the right limits. At B = 0 its eigenvalues are −8Dq and +2Dq, and at large Dq the B-dependence of the t₂² ³T₁ level is 3B, as expected.\n\n**Solution.**\n1. ν₃ and ν₁ differ by exactly 10Dq, because ³A₂g and ³T₂g are not mixed: ν₃ − ν₁ = 12Dq − 2Dq. So 10Dq = 32 750 − 15 730 = 17 020 cm⁻¹, which gives Dq ≈ 1702 cm⁻¹.\n2. From ν₁ = 2Dq − E₋, the ground state is E₋ = 3404 − 15 730 = −12 326 cm⁻¹.\n3. Put E₋ into the secular equation (−10 212 − E₋)(15B − E₋) = (6808)². The first factor is 2114, so 15B + 12 326 ≈ 21 930. This gives 15B ≈ 9600, so B ≈ 640 cm⁻¹.\n4. Check on ν₂: E₊ = (−10 212 + 9600) + 12 326 ≈ 11 714 cm⁻¹. Then ν₂ = E₊ − E₋ ≈ 24 040 cm⁻¹, which matches the observed 24 030 cm⁻¹.\n\nThe fit is self-consistent. B ≈ 640 cm⁻¹ is about 60% of the free-ion value for a typical d² ion. C is not determined, because spin-forbidden bands are not given.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1702, \"B\": 640, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three spin-allowed bands of d2 Oh fit Dq and B via the 3T1g(F)/3T1g(P) mixing matrix; C is not determinable.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":806,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transforma